# Not a real moz.build — this is a diff note for the ONE line that must
# change in the upstream file netwerk/protocol/moz.build (outside this
# pyxis/ patch directory) to wire in netwerk/protocol/pyxis/.
#
# Verified against the real pinned tree (ESR 140.0.5,
# target/gecko-src/gecko-dev/netwerk/protocol/moz.build), current content:
#
#   DIRS += ["about", "data", "file"]
#   if CONFIG["MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT"] == "gtk":
#       DIRS += ["gio"]
#   DIRS += ["http", "res", "viewsource", "websocket", "webtransport"]
#
# Required change (add "pyxis" to the unconditional DIRS list — Pyxis is not
# gtk-only in the way gio's D-Bus/GVFS integration is, so it belongs in the
# unconditional list alongside http/res/etc.):
#
#   DIRS += ["about", "data", "file"]
#   if CONFIG["MOZ_WIDGET_TOOLKIT"] == "gtk":
#       DIRS += ["gio"]
#   DIRS += ["http", "pyxis", "res", "viewsource", "websocket", "webtransport"]
#
# Apply with (from the gecko-dev checkout root):
#   sed -i 's/DIRS += \["http", "res"/DIRS += ["http", "pyxis", "res"/' \
#       netwerk/protocol/moz.build
# then verify by hand (sed one-liners against upstream files are worth a
# manual diff check after every ESR rebase, since the exact line contents
# may shift).
